<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Griffith Joyner is a 36-year-old former Olympic sprinter with focal epilepsy from a left orbitofrontal cavernous malformation, removed completely ten weeks ago, who comes for her yearly preventive visit. She has had no seizure since the one on the flight four and a half months ago. She takes levetiracetam twice a day and folic acid daily and has missed no doses; the early irritability has gone. She is running and doing sprint drills again, swims only with a companion, and wears her seizure detection watch at night. She is not driving. She is not planning a pregnancy in the next year. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Periodic adult preventive visit, age 36</td></tr><tr><td>Epilepsy</td><td>No seizure since the flight; levetiracetam taken as prescribed</td></tr><tr><td>Surgery</td><td>Lesionectomy ten weeks ago; scar healed</td></tr><tr><td>Mood</td><td>PHQ-2 0</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient on the clinic&apos;s online form before the visit and reviewed with her by Dr. Vanterpool. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Very good</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Busy with design work and youth fitness programs; good supports; some worry about seizures in public, less than before</td></tr><tr><td>Substance use</td><td>No tobacco; alcohol rarely; no drug use</td></tr><tr><td>Physical activity</td><td>Training five or six days a week: running, sprint drills and weights</td></tr><tr><td>Nutrition</td><td>Balanced diet planned around training; folic acid daily</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Seven to eight hours at regular times; detection watch worn at night</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>Seat belt always as a passenger; not driving; showers rather than baths; swims only with a companion; smoke alarms tested</td></tr><tr><td>Intimate partner violence</td><td>Screened privately with a validated tool: negative</td></tr><tr><td>Reproductive plans</td><td>No pregnancy planned in the next year; contraception reviewed</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

