    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Periodic adult preventive visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and the prevention plan updated. Cervical screening with cytology and HPV co-testing done today. HIV, hepatitis C and hepatitis B screening drawn today. No pregnancy planned; folic acid continues because she takes an antiseizure medication and could become pregnant. Intimate partner violence screen negative. [S]<list><item>Results by phone.</item><item>Influenza and COVID-19 vaccines this autumn.</item><item>Mammogram from 40.</item><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Focal epilepsy with structural cause, seizure-free after lesionectomy (G40.209)</content>. No seizure in four and a half months and none since surgery; levetiracetam tolerated. [S]<list><item>Continue levetiracetam 500 mg twice daily and folic acid.</item><item>Driving review at the six-month visit.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blood pressure screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>110/70 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 0; PHQ-9 4 five weeks ago</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Rare use</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco use</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Never</td></tr><tr><td>Intimate partner violence screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Screened privately; negative</td></tr><tr><td>Cervical cancer screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Cytology with HPV co-testing, with a chaperone</td></tr><tr><td>Breast cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Mammography from 40</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Begins at 45</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Age 36 with a BMI of 21.0 and no risk factor</td></tr><tr><td>HIV, hepatitis C and hepatitis B screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Once-in-adulthood screening drawn today</td></tr><tr><td>Folic acid for a woman who could become pregnant</td><td>Up to date</td><td>0.4 mg daily, started with levetiracetam</td></tr><tr><td>Tdap</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No dose recorded in the past ten years</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza and COVID-19 vaccines, this season</td><td>Due</td><td>This autumn, when the season&apos;s vaccines arrive</td></tr><tr><td>Dental and eye examinations</td><td>Due</td><td>Dental review and an eye examination advised this year</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Tetanus, diphtheria, and acellular pertussis vaccine (Tdap) [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: Depression and Suicide Risk in Adults: Screening (2023); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Breast Cancer: Screening (2024); Cervical Cancer: Screening (2018); Intimate Partner Violence and Caregiver Abuse of Older or Vulnerable Adults: Screening (2025); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Cervical screening and blood test results by phone. Six-month epilepsy review in October with the driving review. Influenza and COVID-19 vaccines this autumn. Next preventive visit in one year. Next scheduled visit 2026-10-20: six months after the seizure: seizure freedom, driving review, training, and the long-term plan. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
